1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:06,563
Next up is the mathematical bridge the mathematical bridge leans across the river cam connecting two parts of queens college.
接下来是数学桥。数学桥横跨康河，连接王后学院的两个部分。

2
00:00:06,563 --> 00:00:13,480
This famous bridge is rumored to have been designed by sir isaac newton without using any nuts or bolts.
据传，这座著名的桥由艾萨克·牛顿爵士设计，建造时没有使用任何螺母或螺栓。

3
00:00:13,480 --> 00:00:19,998
The story goes that university students or fellows then took the bridge apart only to fail at putting it back together.
故事是这样的：大学里的学生或研究员把桥拆开，结果却没能把它重新组装起来。

4
00:00:19,998 --> 00:00:24,840
They then had to resort to rebuilding it using nuts and bolts leaving the bridge as it stands today.
他们于是只好用螺母和螺栓重建它，就成了今天这座桥的样子。

5
00:00:25,560 --> 00:00:32,383
While this is nothing more than a popular myth there is no denying that this arch bridge built with straight timbers is a really interesting design.
虽然这只是个流传很广的传说，但用笔直木料建成的拱桥，设计确实很有意思。

6
00:00:32,383 --> 00:00:36,154
You will almost certainly be shown this bridge if you go on a guided tour.
如果参加导览，导游几乎肯定会带你看这座桥。

7
00:00:36,154 --> 00:00:38,440
But if you don't then be sure to look out for it.
如果不参加，也一定记得留意这座桥。

8
00:00:41,240 --> 00:00:45,640
Number six has to be one of my cambridge favorites and that is to visit the botanic garden.
第六项一定算是我在剑桥最喜欢的活动之一，那就是参观植物园。

9
00:00:46,280 --> 00:00:54,760
The cambridge university botanic garden has a really impressive collection of over 8000 plant species from around the world to assist with teaching and research.
剑桥大学植物园收藏了来自世界各地的八千多种植物，用来辅助教学和研究，令人印象深刻。

10
00:00:56,040 --> 00:01:01,898
At 40 acres the garden is surprisingly large so on average guests spend around two to three hours there.
作者介绍，植物园占地四十英亩，比想象中大，因此游客平均会在那里待两到三小时。

11
00:01:01,898 --> 00:01:05,480
We were there for at least three hours probably a fair bit longer.
我们在那里至少待了三小时，大概还要更久一些。

12
00:01:06,680 --> 00:01:10,280
The lush gardens have been designed so that they're worth visiting all year round.
这些郁郁葱葱的花园经过设计，一年四季都值得来看看。

13
00:01:10,840 --> 00:01:15,640
We visited in summer and the beds of colourful flowers were in full bloom and looked incredible.
我们在夏天去的，花坛里五颜六色的花正盛开着，看起来美极了。

14
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:24,451
Our favorite part of the botanical garden had to be the glass houses packed wall to wall with a diverse range of plants from different habitats.
我们最喜欢的部分，一定是那些温室，里面从这头到那头，满满都是来自不同生境的各类植物。

15
00:01:24,451 --> 00:01:29,720
You'll see cacti from america and africa exotic plants from the tropical rainforests and wetlands.
你会看到来自美洲和非洲的仙人掌，以及来自热带雨林和湿地的奇异植物，

16
00:01:29,720 --> 00:01:33,772
And species from as far as south australia and the oceanic islands.
还有来自遥远的南澳大利亚和大洋洲岛屿的物种。

17
00:01:33,772 --> 00:01:42,280
If you have even a small level of interest in visiting gardens then cambridge university botanic garden is definitely a good one for your itinerary.
如果你对逛花园哪怕有一点兴趣，剑桥大学植物园都绝对值得加入你的行程。

18
00:01:44,920 --> 00:01:53,320
Number seven is climb great saint mary's church tower for one of the best if not the best viewpoints in cambridge head to great st mary's church.
第七项，是爬上大圣玛丽教堂的塔楼。要寻找剑桥最好的观景点之一，甚至可能是最好的，就去大圣玛丽教堂。

19
00:01:53,320 --> 00:02:00,040
When you pay your admission you'll be given a useful leaflet to help you identify the different landmarks you can see from the top.
作者说，买门票时会拿到一份实用的小册子，帮助你辨认从塔顶能看到的不同地标。

20
00:02:00,040 --> 00:02:03,720
Enjoy the bird's eye view of several of the magnificent college buildings.
从这里俯瞰几座宏伟的学院建筑，

21
00:02:03,720 --> 00:02:07,800
And partake in some very long distance people watching in the lively market square.
还可以远远地观察热闹集市广场上来来往往的人们。

22
00:02:08,520 --> 00:02:12,680
The climb up and down the tower is narrow and steep so be prepared for that.
上下塔楼的通道狭窄而陡峭，所以要有心理准备。

23
00:02:12,680 --> 00:02:15,944
But if you are okay with steps then it's totally worth it.
不过，如果你能适应爬台阶，那完全值得。

24
00:02:15,944 --> 00:02:22,520
Before you leave make sure you take a walk around the church itself and get a closer look at those beautiful stained glass windows.
离开前，一定在教堂里走一走，近距离看看那些漂亮的彩色玻璃窗。

25
00:02:25,640 --> 00:02:29,880
One of the things we loved about cambridge is that you're never far from a green space.
我们很喜欢剑桥的一点，是在这里总有绿地离你不远。

26
00:02:29,880 --> 00:02:35,969
Let's start with jesus green which is a spacious park in the north of central cambridge and is the perfect place for a picnic.
先说 Jesus Green，它是剑桥市中心北边的一座宽阔公园，非常适合野餐。

27
00:02:35,969 --> 00:02:40,973
If the weather is warm on your visit then you might be happy to learn there's also a lido.
如果你去的时候天气暖和，那么知道这里还有露天泳池，可能会让你很高兴。

28
00:02:40,973 --> 00:02:46,722
After lolling in the grass or swimming in the lido you could stretch your legs with a stroll along the bordering river.
在草地上懒洋洋地躺一会儿，或在泳池里游完泳后，可以沿着公园边的河流散步，活动一下腿脚。

29
00:02:46,722 --> 00:02:51,800
Follow the river to reach the adjacent midsummer common where you could see the iconic cambridge cows.
沿河走就能到相邻的 Midsummer Common，在那里可以看到标志性的剑桥牛群。

30
00:02:52,680 --> 00:03:00,680
There's a tradition going back centuries where farmers would bring their cows to graze in the city commons these much loved cows even have their own twitter account.
这里有延续了数百年的传统：农民会带牛到城市公用草地上吃草。作者还说，这些备受喜爱的牛甚至有自己的 Twitter 账号。

31
00:03:03,160 --> 00:03:06,840
Parker's piece is another large green common area near the centre of cambridge.
Parker's Piece 是剑桥中心附近另一大片绿色公用草地。

32
00:03:08,040 --> 00:03:13,069
At the crossroads near the middle of the park you'll see a late 10 th century large cast iron lamppost.
在公园中部附近的交叉路口，你会看到一根大型铸铁灯柱；原字幕称其年代为“十世纪晚期”，这一年代待听辨核实。

33
00:03:13,069 --> 00:03:17,000
Nicknamed by the students in the 1960 s as reality checkpoint.
在二十世纪六十年代，学生给它起了个绰号，叫“现实检查点”。

34
00:03:19,640 --> 00:03:24,288
Walk to the top of castle mound this spot is all that remains of cambridge castle.
再走到 Castle Mound 的顶部；这里就是剑桥城堡仅存的地方。

35
00:03:24,288 --> 00:03:29,480
Which was built in the 11 th century by william the conqueror to control the route to the north of England.
据作者介绍，那座城堡是征服者威廉在十一世纪修建的，用来控制通往英格兰北部的路线。

36
00:03:29,480 --> 00:03:34,424
There might not really be anything left to see but from the top of the mound you'll have a good view over the city.
这里可能确实没剩下什么可看的，但从土丘顶上，你能很好地眺望整座城市。

37
00:03:34,424 --> 00:03:39,968
It's perhaps not somewhere to go out of your way for but worth stopping by if you're in the area.
或许不值得特地绕路来一趟，但如果你就在附近，顺便停下来看看还是值得的。
